WEBVTT

00:06.840 --> 00:09.259
[rain falling]

00:09.342 --> 00:11.678
[thunder rumbling]

00:12.846 --> 00:14.681
[breathing heavily]

00:14.764 --> 00:16.766
[Mike] Is there a number we can call
for your parents?

00:16.850 --> 00:18.935
Where's your hair?
Do you have cancer?

00:19.019 --> 00:20.228
[Lucas] Did you run away?

00:20.311 --> 00:22.230
- Are you in some kind of trouble?
- Is that blood?

00:23.022 --> 00:25.108
- Stop it! You're freaking her out!
- She's freaking me out!

00:25.191 --> 00:26.401
I bet she's deaf.

00:28.486 --> 00:29.571
Not deaf.

00:29.654 --> 00:32.949
All right, that's enough, all right?
She's just scared and cold.

00:36.536 --> 00:37.912
[thunder rumbles]

00:39.581 --> 00:41.416
Here, these are clean.
Okay?

00:52.135 --> 00:53.386
- No, no, no!
- [boys exclaiming]

00:53.470 --> 00:55.096
[Dustin] Oh, my God.
Oh, my God.

00:55.180 --> 00:58.433
See over there?
[stammers] That's the bathroom.

00:58.516 --> 01:00.518
Privacy.
Get it?

01:15.742 --> 01:16.910
You don't want it closed?

01:18.745 --> 01:19.746
No.

01:19.829 --> 01:21.915
Oh, so you can speak.

01:21.998 --> 01:24.209
Okay, well...

01:24.292 --> 01:28.296
Um, how about we just keep the door...

01:30.548 --> 01:32.133
just like this.

01:32.634 --> 01:35.345
- Is that better?
- Yes.

01:40.975 --> 01:43.102
[Dustin] This is mental.
[Mike] At least she can talk.

01:43.186 --> 01:46.064
She said "no" and "yes."
Your three-year-old sister says more.

01:46.147 --> 01:47.857
She tried to get naked.

01:47.941 --> 01:49.567
There's something
seriously wrong with her.

01:49.651 --> 01:53.154
- Like, wrong in the head.
- She just went like...

01:53.238 --> 01:54.697
I bet she escaped from Pennhurst.

01:54.781 --> 01:57.408
- From where?
- The nuthouse in Kerley County.

01:57.492 --> 01:59.119
- You got a lot of family there?
- Bite me.

01:59.202 --> 02:01.204
Seriously though, think about it.

02:01.287 --> 02:04.332
That would explain her shaved hair
and why she's so crazy.

02:04.415 --> 02:05.542
[Dustin] Why she went like...

02:05.625 --> 02:08.419
She's an escapee is the point.
She's probably a psycho.

02:08.503 --> 02:10.505
- Like Michael Myers.
- [Lucas] Exactly!

02:10.588 --> 02:12.173
We should've never brought her here.

02:12.257 --> 02:13.591
So you just wanted to leave her
out in that storm?

02:13.675 --> 02:16.427
Yes! We went out to find Will,
not another problem.

02:16.511 --> 02:18.221
- I think we should tell your mom.
- I second that.

02:18.304 --> 02:20.265
- Who's crazy now?
- How is that crazy?

02:20.348 --> 02:22.934
'Cause, we weren't supposed to be
out tonight, remember?

02:23.017 --> 02:25.353
- So?
- So if I tell my mom

02:25.436 --> 02:27.272
and she tells your mom
and your mom...

02:27.355 --> 02:29.607
- Oh, man.
- Our houses become Alcatraz.

02:29.691 --> 02:32.277
Exactly.
We'll never find Will.

02:34.028 --> 02:36.573
All right, here's the plan.
She sleeps here tonight.

02:36.656 --> 02:38.783
- You're letting a girl--
- Just listen!

02:38.867 --> 02:40.827
In the morning,
she sneaks around my house,

02:40.910 --> 02:42.954
goes to the front door
and rings my doorbell.

02:43.037 --> 02:44.831
My mom will answer and know
exactly what to do.

02:44.914 --> 02:47.167
She'll send her back to Pennhurst
or wherever she comes from.

02:47.250 --> 02:48.376
We'll be totally in the clear.

02:48.459 --> 02:50.253
And tomorrow night, we go back out.

02:50.336 --> 02:52.714
And this time, we find Will.

02:57.343 --> 02:59.345
Here you go.
This is my sleeping bag.

02:59.429 --> 03:01.723
[Dustin] You really think she's psycho?

03:01.806 --> 03:03.391
Wouldn't want her in my house.

03:07.812 --> 03:09.439
[sighs] Mental.

03:11.608 --> 03:13.776
Hey, um, I never asked your name.

03:13.860 --> 03:15.111
[door closes]

03:21.242 --> 03:22.493
Is that real?

03:25.330 --> 03:29.584
Sorry, I've just... never seen
a kid with a tattoo before.

03:30.418 --> 03:32.211
What's it mean?
Eleven?

03:35.548 --> 03:36.674
That's your name?

03:38.801 --> 03:40.845
Eleven. Okay.

03:40.929 --> 03:44.265
Um, well, my name's Mike.
Short for Michael.

03:44.349 --> 03:47.560
Maybe we can call you "El."
Short for Eleven.

03:51.606 --> 03:53.024
Um, well, okay.

03:53.942 --> 03:55.193
'Night, El.

03:57.445 --> 03:58.738
'Night, Mike.

04:16.172 --> 04:18.007
[door opens and closes]

04:23.137 --> 04:24.889
[thunder rumbling]

04:37.527 --> 04:39.529
[theme music playing]

05:53.144 --> 05:56.814
All right, Mom.
Breakfast is ready.

05:56.898 --> 05:59.692
- What? No, be careful of the poster.
- Yeah, okay. All right.

05:59.776 --> 06:01.652
- I can't eat.
- I just need you to eat, Mom.

06:01.736 --> 06:05.156
[sniffles] Listen. Listen, the Xerox place
opens in, like, 30 minutes.

06:05.239 --> 06:06.657
- Yeah.
- And I don't want you to go alone...

06:06.741 --> 06:07.825
No, I know.
I told you, I got it.

06:07.909 --> 06:10.328
...so I'm gonna have Karen take you,
'cause I should be here.

06:10.411 --> 06:12.789
- Okay.
- We need to make, what, 200, 300 copies?

06:12.872 --> 06:13.998
- How much is a copy?
- Yeah, okay.

06:14.082 --> 06:15.166
- Okay, Mom. Mom.
- Ten cents?

06:15.249 --> 06:17.877
- [stammering] If we... Ten cents--
- Mom. Mom. Mom!

06:17.960 --> 06:20.213
[stutters] You can't get like this, okay?

06:20.296 --> 06:22.715
- I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
- No, it's okay.

06:22.799 --> 06:24.342
[knocking on door]

06:25.301 --> 06:28.596
[sighs] We've been waiting six hours.

06:28.679 --> 06:30.389
I know.
I came as soon as I could.

06:30.473 --> 06:32.058
Six hours.

06:32.141 --> 06:34.268
A little bit of trust here, all right?

06:34.352 --> 06:37.313
We've been searching all night.
Went all the way to Cartersville.

06:37.396 --> 06:39.065
- And?
- Nothing.

06:39.148 --> 06:40.566
God.

06:43.236 --> 06:44.654
Flo says you got a phone call?

06:44.737 --> 06:46.906
Oh, yeah.

06:48.407 --> 06:49.617
[Joyce sniffles]

06:54.205 --> 06:55.832
[Hopper] Storm barbecued this pretty good.

06:55.915 --> 06:58.334
- The storm?
- What else?

06:58.417 --> 07:01.337
You're saying that that's not weird?

07:01.420 --> 07:03.089
No, it's weird.

07:03.172 --> 07:05.675
Can we, like, trace who made the call?
Contact the--

07:05.758 --> 07:07.760
No, it doesn't work like that.

07:07.844 --> 07:09.595
Now, uh, you're sure it was Will?

07:09.679 --> 07:11.347
Because Flo said
you just heard some breathing.

07:11.431 --> 07:14.475
No. It was him.
It was Will.

07:15.476 --> 07:19.522
[voice breaking] And he was scared.
And then something--

07:19.605 --> 07:22.442
It was probably just a prank call.
It was somebody trying to scare you.

07:22.525 --> 07:24.277
- Who would do that?
- Well, this thing's been on TV.

07:24.360 --> 07:27.530
It brings out all the crazies, you know.
False leads, prank calls, uh...

07:27.613 --> 07:30.616
No, Hopper, it was not a prank.
It was him.

07:30.700 --> 07:33.327
- Joyce.
- Come on, how about a little trust here?

07:34.328 --> 07:36.622
What, you think I'm... I'm making this up?

07:36.706 --> 07:38.166
I'm not saying that you're making it up.

07:38.249 --> 07:40.710
All I'm saying is
it's an emotional time for you.

07:40.793 --> 07:44.088
And you think I don't know
my own son's breathing?

07:44.172 --> 07:45.798
Wouldn't you know your own daughter's?

07:57.101 --> 07:58.102
[Joyce sniffles]

07:59.687 --> 08:02.857
- You hear from, uh, Lonnie yet?
- No.

08:03.441 --> 08:05.318
It's been long enough.
I'm having him checked out.

08:05.401 --> 08:07.069
[Joyce sighs] Oh, come on!

08:07.153 --> 08:09.238
You're wasting your time.

08:11.199 --> 08:12.950
Hey, Hopper.

08:13.034 --> 08:15.203
Hopper. [panting]

08:15.286 --> 08:16.537
Let me go.

08:18.164 --> 08:19.957
- I'm sorry?
- To Lonnie's.

08:20.041 --> 08:22.919
[stammering] You know, if Will's there,
it means he ran away.

08:23.002 --> 08:25.421
And if he sees the cops,
he'll think he's in trouble.

08:25.505 --> 08:27.215
He'll... He'll hide.

08:27.298 --> 08:29.008
- You know, he's good at hiding.
- Yeah?

08:30.176 --> 08:32.428
Well, cops are good at finding.
Okay?

08:32.512 --> 08:34.180
Stay here with your mom.

08:35.389 --> 08:36.474
She needs you.

08:41.145 --> 08:42.563
[engine starting]

08:43.940 --> 08:45.483
[music playing faintly on TV]

08:55.201 --> 08:57.828
Slow down, Mike.
That's disgusting.

08:59.288 --> 09:01.165
Do a lot of studying last night?

09:01.916 --> 09:03.834
Yeah, actually, I did.

09:03.918 --> 09:06.295
What was your test on again?
Human anatomy?

09:08.339 --> 09:10.091
Hey, what's going on?

09:11.384 --> 09:12.593
[both] Nothing.

09:15.304 --> 09:16.806
[radio static]

09:16.889 --> 09:18.641
[footsteps approaching]

09:24.021 --> 09:25.398
Hey, you found my supercomm.

09:25.481 --> 09:26.649
Pretty cool, huh?

09:27.316 --> 09:28.609
I talk to my friends with it.

09:28.693 --> 09:30.570
Mostly Lucas,
'cause he lives so close.

09:30.653 --> 09:31.737
Signal's pretty weak.

09:35.950 --> 09:37.118
Got you breakfast.

09:39.704 --> 09:41.664
So listen, this is gonna
sound a little weird,

09:41.747 --> 09:43.082
but I just need you to go out there.

09:43.165 --> 09:45.293
Then go to the front door
and ring the doorbell.

09:45.376 --> 09:48.921
My mom will answer and you'll tell her
that you're lost and that you need help.

09:49.005 --> 09:53.134
But whatever you do, you can't tell her
about last night or that you know me.

09:53.217 --> 09:54.218
Understand?

09:55.344 --> 09:56.721
Really, it's no big deal.

09:56.804 --> 09:58.931
We'll just pretend
to meet each other again.

09:59.932 --> 10:02.602
And my mom, she'll know who to call.

10:05.062 --> 10:06.105
No.

10:07.398 --> 10:08.524
No?

10:09.358 --> 10:10.359
No.

10:11.360 --> 10:14.780
No... you don't want my mom to get help?

10:19.577 --> 10:22.121
You're in trouble, aren't you?

10:25.958 --> 10:27.001
Who...

10:28.461 --> 10:30.129
Who are you in trouble with?

10:32.882 --> 10:34.425
Bad.

10:34.508 --> 10:35.593
Bad?

10:36.594 --> 10:37.762
Bad people?

10:41.432 --> 10:43.476
They want to hurt you?

10:43.559 --> 10:44.977
The bad people?

10:54.737 --> 10:56.405
Understand?

10:57.490 --> 10:59.992
[Karen] Michael, where are you?
We're going to be late.

11:00.076 --> 11:01.786
- Let's go!
- [stammers] All right, I'll be back.

11:01.869 --> 11:03.621
Just stay here, okay?
Stay here.

11:04.705 --> 11:06.374
[footsteps receding]

11:10.961 --> 11:12.380
When was this?

11:12.463 --> 11:14.090
Last night.
Less than two miles away.

11:14.173 --> 11:15.966
- And the boy?
- Still missing.

11:16.717 --> 11:19.762
[Joyce] It was my son.
I know it.

11:19.845 --> 11:22.139
And I... I heard something else.

11:22.223 --> 11:23.599
[Florence] Something else?

11:24.809 --> 11:28.312
[Joyce] It was like, uh,
some kind of animal.

11:28.396 --> 11:31.899
[stammers] I don't know.
Just please tell Hop to hurry.

11:31.982 --> 11:34.902
[volunteers shouting] Will! Will Byers!

11:35.778 --> 11:37.655
[Callahan] Will Byers!

11:37.738 --> 11:39.240
[dog barking]

11:40.199 --> 11:42.493
[Powell] Will!
[volunteers] Will!

11:42.576 --> 11:45.329
[Hopper] Hey!
Anything?

11:46.288 --> 11:47.331
[Callahan] You?

11:48.290 --> 11:50.543
[Hopper] No, nothing but a dead phone.

11:50.626 --> 11:51.627
[Callahan] Joyce?

11:51.710 --> 11:54.463
About one step from falling off the edge.

11:54.547 --> 11:56.966
She's been a few steps
for a while now, hasn't she?

11:57.049 --> 11:58.801
Kid's missing, man.

11:58.884 --> 12:00.177
Show a little class.

12:01.178 --> 12:03.681
All right. Come on, let's go!

12:03.764 --> 12:06.016
We got a lot of ground to cover.

12:06.100 --> 12:08.519
The chief and her,
they've screwed before, huh?

12:11.063 --> 12:12.731
Will!

12:12.815 --> 12:14.275
That a "yeah" or did they...

12:15.317 --> 12:17.403
- Will!
- Will!

12:24.952 --> 12:28.372
"When alpha particles go through
gold foil, they become..."

12:28.456 --> 12:31.000
- Unoccupied space.
- "A molecule that can--"

12:31.083 --> 12:32.168
- Hey!
- [Steve] I don't know,

12:32.251 --> 12:33.544
I think you've studied enough, Nance.

12:33.627 --> 12:35.671
- [Nancy] Steve--
- I'm telling you, you know, you got this.

12:35.754 --> 12:38.090
Don't worry.
Now, on to more important matters.

12:38.174 --> 12:41.135
My dad has left town on a conference
and my mom's gone with him,

12:41.218 --> 12:43.637
- 'cause, you know, she doesn't trust him.
- Good call.

12:43.721 --> 12:44.722
So are you in?

12:44.805 --> 12:46.223
In for what?

12:46.307 --> 12:48.058
No parents? Big house?

12:48.726 --> 12:49.852
A party?

12:49.935 --> 12:51.854
- [Carol] Ding, ding, ding!
- [Tommy laughs]

12:51.979 --> 12:53.397
It's Tuesday.

12:53.481 --> 12:54.940
[mocking] It's Tuesday!
Oh, my God.

12:55.024 --> 12:56.358
- [both laughing]
- Come on.

12:56.442 --> 12:58.194
It'll be low key.
It'll just be us.

12:58.277 --> 13:00.654
What do you say?
Are you in or are you out?

13:00.738 --> 13:04.575
- Um...
- Oh, God. Look.

13:05.576 --> 13:07.286
Oh, God, that's depressing.

13:09.497 --> 13:12.750
- Should we say something?
- I don't think he speaks.

13:12.833 --> 13:14.585
How much you want to bet he killed him?

13:14.668 --> 13:15.920
Shut up.

13:23.219 --> 13:24.720
[Nancy] Hey.

13:24.803 --> 13:26.388
Oh, hey.

13:26.472 --> 13:27.640
I just...

13:28.807 --> 13:32.102
I wanted to say, you know, um...

13:32.186 --> 13:34.104
I'm sorry about everything.

13:39.527 --> 13:41.820
Everyone's thinking about you.

13:43.948 --> 13:46.617
- It sucks.
- Yeah.

13:50.120 --> 13:51.372
I'm sure he's fine.

13:51.455 --> 13:53.123
He's a smart kid.

13:53.207 --> 13:55.000
[school bell ringing]

13:56.043 --> 13:57.920
I have to go.
[chuckles] Chemistry test.

13:58.003 --> 13:59.004
Yeah.

13:59.088 --> 14:00.548
- Good luck.
- Thanks.

14:05.344 --> 14:07.888
[principal on PA]
Attention, faculty and students.

14:07.972 --> 14:11.433
At 8:00 p.m. tonight, there will be
an assembly on the football field

14:11.517 --> 14:13.852
in support of Will Byers and his family.

14:13.936 --> 14:16.063
All are encouraged to attend.

14:16.146 --> 14:20.317
Volunteer sign-ups for search parties
are still available in the office.

14:22.111 --> 14:23.863
[indistinct chatter]

14:26.490 --> 14:27.700
Oh, this is weird.

14:28.158 --> 14:31.161
- He's never this late.
- I'm telling you, his stupid plan failed.

14:31.245 --> 14:32.496
I thought you liked his plan.

14:32.580 --> 14:34.915
Yeah, but obviously it was stupid,
or he'd be here.

14:34.999 --> 14:36.959
If his mom found out
a girl spent the night--

14:37.042 --> 14:38.544
He's in deep shit right about now.

14:38.627 --> 14:41.297
Hey, what if she slept naked?

14:41.380 --> 14:43.299
Oh, my God, she didn't.

14:43.382 --> 14:45.593
Oh, if Mrs. Wheeler tells my parents...

14:45.676 --> 14:48.554
- No way. Mike would never rat us out.
- I don't know.

14:48.637 --> 14:51.849
All that matters is, after school,
the freak will be back in the loony bin,

14:51.932 --> 14:55.060
and we can focus on what really matters,
finding Will.

15:11.201 --> 15:12.411
[Mike] You want anything to drink?

15:12.494 --> 15:15.164
We have OJ, skim milk...
What else?

15:16.498 --> 15:17.875
Um, we have...

15:19.793 --> 15:21.545
Oh, this is my living room.

15:21.629 --> 15:23.172
It's mostly just for watching TV.

15:23.255 --> 15:25.799
Nice, right?
It's a 22-inch.

15:25.883 --> 15:27.968
That's, like, ten times bigger
than Dustin's.

15:39.438 --> 15:41.690
- Pretty.
- I guess.

15:41.774 --> 15:43.192
That's my sister Nancy.

15:43.275 --> 15:44.902
And that's baby Holly.

15:44.985 --> 15:46.362
And those are my parents.

15:47.029 --> 15:48.155
What are your parents like?

15:48.781 --> 15:50.199
Do they live close?

15:52.618 --> 15:54.203
That's our La-Z-Boy.

15:55.913 --> 15:57.164
It's where my dad sleeps.

15:57.247 --> 15:59.959
You can try it if you want.

16:00.626 --> 16:01.627
Yeah.

16:02.962 --> 16:03.963
It's fun.

16:07.591 --> 16:09.426
Just trust me, okay?

16:13.514 --> 16:15.182
- [Mike chuckles]
- [Eleven laughs nervously]

16:15.265 --> 16:16.934
See? Fun, right?

16:18.811 --> 16:19.812
Now you try.

16:25.109 --> 16:26.402
[both laugh]

16:29.905 --> 16:31.907
[rock music playing on car stereo]

16:39.373 --> 16:41.375
["Should I Stay or Should I Go"
playing on stereo]

16:52.845 --> 16:54.388
[song continues playing on stereo]

16:54.471 --> 16:57.224
♪ Darling, you got to let me know ♪

16:58.767 --> 17:02.479
♪ Should I stay or should I go? ♪

17:02.563 --> 17:04.189
- You like it?
- Yeah, it's cool.

17:04.273 --> 17:05.941
All right, you can keep
the mix if you want.

17:06.025 --> 17:07.151
- Really?
- Yeah, really.

17:07.234 --> 17:08.819
All the best stuff's on there.

17:08.902 --> 17:11.822
Joy Division, Bowie, Television,
The Smiths...

17:11.905 --> 17:13.615
It'll totally change your life.

17:13.699 --> 17:15.367
Yeah, totally.

17:15.451 --> 17:17.536
[Joyce faintly]
Where the hell are you, Lonnie?

17:17.619 --> 17:19.079
I don't want to hear it.
I don't want to hear it.

17:19.163 --> 17:21.457
[Joyce muttering indistinctly]

17:23.834 --> 17:27.921
[Joyce] This is ridiculous!
I'm so sick of your excuses.

17:28.005 --> 17:30.799
♪ One day is fine and next is black ♪

17:30.883 --> 17:32.384
- [lowers volume]
- He's not coming, is he?

17:34.094 --> 17:35.471
Do you even like baseball?

17:36.597 --> 17:38.807
No, but... I don't know.

17:38.891 --> 17:40.893
- It's fun to go with him sometimes.
- Come on.

17:40.976 --> 17:43.729
Has he ever done anything with you
that you actually like?

17:43.812 --> 17:45.564
You know, like the arcade or something?

17:46.356 --> 17:49.068
- I don't know.
- No, all right? He hasn't.

17:49.151 --> 17:50.986
He's trying to force you
to like normal things.

17:51.070 --> 17:54.114
And you shouldn't like things because
people tell you you're supposed to.

17:54.198 --> 17:55.491
Okay?

17:56.283 --> 17:57.993
Especially not him.

17:59.870 --> 18:02.247
But you like The Clash? For real?

18:02.331 --> 18:04.458
For real.
Definitely.

18:05.209 --> 18:06.752
[raises volume]

18:06.835 --> 18:09.588
♪ Should I cool it or should I blow? ♪

18:11.215 --> 18:15.594
♪ So you gotta let me know ♪

18:15.677 --> 18:17.554
♪ Should I stay or should I go? ♪

18:21.934 --> 18:24.228
[bell tolling]

18:35.489 --> 18:37.491
[Christmas carol playing]

18:38.784 --> 18:40.202
[bells chiming]

18:41.787 --> 18:44.206
[Donald] Joyce, I wasn't
expecting you today.

18:44.289 --> 18:47.417
- I brought Jeffrey in to cover.
- [stammers] I'm not here to work.

18:47.501 --> 18:48.919
I... [sighs]

18:49.002 --> 18:51.130
The storm last night, I...

18:51.755 --> 18:53.924
[sighs] I need a new phone.

18:54.007 --> 18:55.050
[cash register dings]

18:55.134 --> 18:58.554
Okay, that looks like $22.56.

18:58.637 --> 19:00.430
Uh, yeah, you know, uh...

19:00.514 --> 19:02.808
I gave Jonathan all my money for...

19:02.891 --> 19:04.685
for the copies for the posters.

19:05.686 --> 19:08.147
Uh, I need an advance.

19:09.064 --> 19:10.566
Yes, well, of course.

19:10.649 --> 19:12.234
- Of course.
- [softly] Thank you.

19:14.153 --> 19:15.279
[Joyce sighs]

19:17.156 --> 19:19.658
[stammers] Yeah, uh, I was thinking,
two weeks?

19:21.910 --> 19:23.162
Um...

19:24.955 --> 19:28.292
Yes, I understand, but, you know,
I have to pay Jeffrey for covering--

19:28.375 --> 19:29.376
Donald.

19:29.459 --> 19:32.671
I've been here ten years, right?

19:32.754 --> 19:36.717
Have I ever called in sick
or missed a shift once?

19:36.800 --> 19:40.179
I've worked, uh,
Christmas Eve and Thanksgiving.

19:41.638 --> 19:43.682
[voice breaking] I don't know
where my boy is.

19:43.765 --> 19:44.975
He's gone.

19:45.058 --> 19:49.104
I don't know if I'm...
gonna ever see him again, if he's hurt...

19:50.856 --> 19:52.191
[sighs] I, uh...

19:53.734 --> 19:57.446
I need this phone
and two weeks' advance.

20:01.074 --> 20:02.826
And a pack of Camels.

20:13.170 --> 20:15.130
- We're all clear.
- [man] Copy that.

20:32.564 --> 20:34.066
[devices beeping]

20:55.754 --> 20:57.464
[beeping continues]

21:01.718 --> 21:03.929
- [beeping rapidly]
- [oozing]

21:12.479 --> 21:14.106
Extraordinary.

21:16.400 --> 21:17.401
[Mike grunts]

21:17.484 --> 21:19.945
[mimicking Yoda] Ready are you?
What knows you of ready?

21:20.028 --> 21:21.321
[in normal voice] His name's Yoda.

21:21.405 --> 21:24.533
He can use the Force to move things
with his mind, like this.

21:24.616 --> 21:25.951
Whoosh!

21:27.703 --> 21:29.413
Oh, this is my dinosaur, Rory.

21:29.496 --> 21:31.331
Look, he has a speaker in his mouth
so he can roar.

21:31.415 --> 21:33.542
[Rory roaring]

21:40.090 --> 21:42.384
Oh, these are all my
science fair trophies.

21:42.467 --> 21:44.803
We got first every year.

21:44.886 --> 21:47.597
Except for last year when we got third.

21:47.681 --> 21:49.766
Mr. Clarke said it was totally political.

22:09.745 --> 22:10.871
You know Will?

22:11.913 --> 22:16.043
Did you see him? Last night?
On the road?

22:17.127 --> 22:18.754
[vehicle approaching]

22:22.549 --> 22:23.717
We gotta go.

22:27.262 --> 22:29.306
[Karen] I bought pizza
and macaroni.

22:29.389 --> 22:30.932
[Holly] Okay.
[Karen] Okay.

22:34.436 --> 22:36.563
Ted? Is that you?

22:36.646 --> 22:37.856
Just me, Mom!

22:37.939 --> 22:40.609
- Mike? What are you doing home?
- One second!

22:45.030 --> 22:46.948
In here.
I'll be right back, okay?

22:47.032 --> 22:49.743
Please, you have to get in,
or my mom, she'll find you.

22:49.826 --> 22:51.787
Do you understand?

22:51.870 --> 22:53.455
I won't tell her about you.
I promise.

22:53.538 --> 22:54.915
Promise?

22:54.998 --> 22:57.000
It means something that you can't break.

22:57.084 --> 22:59.002
- Ever.
- [Karen] Michael?

22:59.628 --> 23:00.670
Please?

23:00.754 --> 23:02.339
[sighs]

23:07.886 --> 23:09.596
[breathing heavily]

23:18.438 --> 23:19.731
[Eleven echoing] Pop!

23:21.733 --> 23:23.860
[sobbing]

23:23.944 --> 23:25.278
[normal] Papa!

23:26.571 --> 23:27.864
Papa!

23:27.948 --> 23:29.282
No!

23:30.200 --> 23:31.326
Papa!

23:31.409 --> 23:33.745
No! No!
No!

23:34.371 --> 23:35.872
[screams]

23:38.542 --> 23:39.584
Papa!

23:39.668 --> 23:41.336
- Papa!
- [banging on door]

23:41.419 --> 23:42.838
Papa!

23:42.921 --> 23:45.006
[sobbing] Papa!

23:45.090 --> 23:46.258
[echoing] Papa!

23:46.341 --> 23:47.717
[sobs]

23:49.845 --> 23:50.887
Papa.

23:55.892 --> 23:57.185
[sobbing]

24:00.480 --> 24:02.899
I just... I don't feel good.

24:02.983 --> 24:05.652
I woke up and my head,
it really hurt bad,

24:05.735 --> 24:07.946
and my throat was all scratchy,
and I wanted to tell you,

24:08.029 --> 24:09.406
but the last time I told you I was sick

24:09.489 --> 24:11.408
- you made me go to school anyway, and--
- Michael.

24:11.491 --> 24:14.327
- Yeah?
- I'm not mad at you.

24:14.411 --> 24:17.706
- No?
- No, of course not.

24:18.582 --> 24:19.958
[sighs]

24:20.041 --> 24:22.961
All this that's been going on with Will,

24:23.044 --> 24:25.172
I can't imagine
what it's been like for you.

24:26.506 --> 24:27.966
I just...

24:28.508 --> 24:30.510
I want you to feel like
you can talk to me.

24:30.594 --> 24:34.347
I never want you to feel like you have
to hide anything from me.

24:34.431 --> 24:36.558
I'm here for you. Okay?

24:37.517 --> 24:38.560
[thud]

24:39.144 --> 24:40.312
Is there someone else here?

24:42.022 --> 24:43.023
No.

24:45.150 --> 24:46.526
Eleven?

24:46.610 --> 24:48.195
Is everything okay?

24:48.278 --> 24:49.321
El?

24:53.742 --> 24:55.702
- [sobs] Mike.
- Is everything okay?

24:55.785 --> 24:56.995
[inhales]

24:58.663 --> 25:00.123
Are you sure?

25:01.416 --> 25:02.792
Promise.

25:15.555 --> 25:17.140
[dial tone]

25:29.569 --> 25:30.612
[grunts]

25:34.115 --> 25:35.450
[exhales]

25:38.828 --> 25:42.332
[volunteer 1] Will Byers!
[volunteer 2] Will!

25:44.542 --> 25:45.961
[Hopper] Whoa, whoa.
Careful, careful.

25:46.044 --> 25:48.255
I need you alive for the next few days,
at least.

25:48.338 --> 25:50.590
[Callahan] Oh, hell, I could survive that.

25:50.674 --> 25:51.675
[Hopper laughs]

25:51.758 --> 25:53.802
[Callahan] What?
George Burness made the jump.

25:53.885 --> 25:56.221
And he was drunk as a skunk.
He did it on a $10 bet.

25:56.304 --> 25:57.305
George is a liar.

25:57.389 --> 26:00.267
You make that jump from this height,
that water turns into cement.

26:00.350 --> 26:02.852
Hits you like a ton of bricks.
Break every damn bone in your body.

26:05.939 --> 26:07.148
Nah.

26:07.232 --> 26:09.025
[Florence on radio] Chief, you copy?

26:10.610 --> 26:12.112
Yeah, Flo, talk to me.

26:12.195 --> 26:14.948
Hey, Chief, we got a call
from over at Benny's.

26:15.031 --> 26:16.866
I think you need to get there right away.

26:21.204 --> 26:23.581
[indistinct radio chatter]

26:34.092 --> 26:35.719
[siren wailing]

26:39.806 --> 26:41.308
Ugh, Jesus!

26:41.391 --> 26:42.642
[flies buzzing]

26:47.480 --> 26:48.606
Suicide?

26:50.066 --> 26:51.568
Mmm-hmm.

26:51.651 --> 26:53.737
[Callahan] Missing kid, suicide...

26:53.820 --> 26:56.531
You must feel like a big city cop again,
huh, Chief?

26:58.241 --> 27:00.994
Well, I mostly dealt
with strangers back then.

27:03.455 --> 27:05.248
Benny was my friend.

27:13.465 --> 27:15.592
[music playing on car stereo]

27:36.196 --> 27:38.239
[music playing on TV]

27:42.035 --> 27:43.328
Hello?

27:43.411 --> 27:44.537
[banging on door]

27:44.621 --> 27:45.830
[Cynthia] Yeah.

27:48.958 --> 27:51.252
- Can I help you?
- Yeah, is Lonnie around?

27:51.336 --> 27:53.338
- Yeah, he's out back. What do you want?
- To look around.

27:53.421 --> 27:55.924
- Hey, what do you think you're doing? Hey!
- I'll be fast.

27:56.007 --> 27:57.342
[Jonathan] Hey, Will?

27:57.425 --> 27:58.802
Will!

27:58.885 --> 28:00.970
Will, you here?
Will!

28:04.307 --> 28:05.809
[grunts]

28:05.892 --> 28:07.102
Get off!

28:08.269 --> 28:09.854
Damn, you've gotten stronger.

28:09.938 --> 28:12.065
Will someone please explain
what the hell is going on?

28:13.024 --> 28:16.319
Jonathan, Cynthia.
Cynthia, this is Jonathan.

28:16.403 --> 28:17.404
My oldest.

28:19.489 --> 28:22.367
- Come here.
- Get off me, man.

28:32.043 --> 28:33.169
[door closes]

28:35.547 --> 28:37.841
- Are you out of your mind?
- Just listen to me.

28:37.924 --> 28:39.718
- You are out of your mind!
- She knows about Will.

28:39.801 --> 28:41.511
What do you mean she knows about Will?

28:42.637 --> 28:45.682
She pointed at him, at his picture.
She knew he was missing. I could tell.

28:45.765 --> 28:47.642
- [Lucas] You could tell?
- Just think about it.

28:47.726 --> 28:49.936
Do you really think it was a coincidence
that we found her on Mirkwood,

28:50.019 --> 28:51.646
the same place where Will disappeared?

28:51.730 --> 28:54.023
- That is weird.
- And she said bad people are after her.

28:54.107 --> 28:57.402
I think maybe these bad people
are the same ones that took Will.

28:57.485 --> 29:00.864
- I think she knows what happened to him.
- Then why doesn't she tell us?

29:03.032 --> 29:05.076
Do you know where he is?

29:05.160 --> 29:06.161
[loudly] Do you know where Will is?

29:06.244 --> 29:08.580
- Stop it, you're scaring her!
- She should be scared!

29:08.663 --> 29:11.541
If you know where he is, tell us!

29:12.876 --> 29:15.420
This is nuts.
We have to take her to your mom.

29:15.503 --> 29:17.922
No! Eleven said telling any adult
would put us in danger.

29:18.006 --> 29:20.425
- What kind of danger?
- Her name is Eleven?

29:20.508 --> 29:23.011
- El for short.
- Mike, what kind of danger?

29:23.094 --> 29:24.721
Danger danger.

29:30.560 --> 29:32.479
No, no, no!

29:32.562 --> 29:35.315
We're going back to plan A.
We're telling your mom.

29:46.910 --> 29:47.994
No.

29:54.209 --> 29:56.920
[Lonnie] Take a look at this beaut.
Should've seen it when I got it.

29:57.003 --> 29:58.880
Took me a year, but it's almost done.

29:59.881 --> 30:02.759
Really?
You want to check up my ass, too?

30:03.426 --> 30:05.261
I told you the same thing
as I told those cops,

30:05.345 --> 30:06.930
he's not here and he never has been.

30:07.013 --> 30:10.016
- Then why didn't you call Mom back?
- I don't know, I just...

30:10.099 --> 30:12.602
I assumed she just forgot where he was.

30:12.685 --> 30:14.229
You know, he was lost or something.

30:15.271 --> 30:17.565
That boy never was very good
at taking care of himself.

30:17.649 --> 30:20.777
This isn't some joke, all right?
There are search parties, reporters...

30:20.860 --> 30:22.195
Hopper's not still chief, is he?

30:24.322 --> 30:27.408
Tell your mother
she's gotta get you out of that hellhole.

30:27.492 --> 30:29.452
Come out here to the city.

30:29.536 --> 30:31.162
People are more real here, you know?

30:32.539 --> 30:33.957
And then I could see you more.

30:36.125 --> 30:38.586
- What, you think I don't want to see you?
- I know you don't.

30:38.670 --> 30:40.713
See, that's your mother talkin'
right there.

30:41.965 --> 30:43.091
She even know you're here?

30:44.133 --> 30:45.134
Oh, great.

30:45.218 --> 30:47.929
So one kid goes missing,
the other one runs wild?

30:48.012 --> 30:49.806
Some real fine parenting right there.

30:49.889 --> 30:53.643
Look, all I'm saying is,
maybe I'm not the asshole, all right?

30:58.356 --> 31:00.024
In case you forgot what he looks like.

31:03.611 --> 31:05.363
[Cynthia] He's kinda cute, hmm?

31:05.446 --> 31:07.490
Maybe I'll trade you in
for the younger model?

31:09.951 --> 31:11.494
[Earl] Just doesn't make any sense, Chief.

31:15.039 --> 31:16.457
You, uh, notice anything...

31:17.500 --> 31:18.877
odd about him the last few weeks?

31:18.960 --> 31:22.213
No, we're fixin' to go fishing
down the Etowah next Sunday.

31:22.297 --> 31:24.424
I mean, he was lookin' forward to it.
I know that.

31:24.507 --> 31:26.718
He got any enemies you might know about?

31:26.801 --> 31:28.887
I mean,
people who might not want him around?

31:28.970 --> 31:31.973
[sighs] The exes didn't like him much.
That's for sure, but...

31:32.974 --> 31:34.517
nah.

31:34.601 --> 31:38.354
- When was the last time you saw him?
- Yesterday. Lunch, same as always.

31:38.438 --> 31:40.690
- Just you and the boys?
- Yep.

31:40.773 --> 31:42.859
Me and Henry and... [sighs]

31:44.152 --> 31:46.696
Well, there was this, uh, this kid.

31:47.697 --> 31:48.823
No kid did this.

31:49.782 --> 31:50.825
Kid?

31:52.243 --> 31:53.703
What are you talking about?

31:53.786 --> 31:58.708
Yeah. At lunch, uh,
there was this boy that, uh...

31:58.791 --> 32:01.544
I mean, he was trying to steal
food out of Benny's kitchen.

32:01.628 --> 32:03.004
Can you imagine that?

32:05.965 --> 32:07.008
This kid...

32:08.635 --> 32:09.761
what'd he look like?

32:10.929 --> 32:14.223
Well, he was about yea high.
You know, tiny like.

32:14.307 --> 32:16.684
I didn't get a good look at him, though.
He was back in the kitchen.

32:16.768 --> 32:18.227
He look like this?

32:19.020 --> 32:21.940
Oh, no, that's...
That's Lonnie's missin' kid.

32:22.023 --> 32:24.067
No. This was a different kid.

32:24.150 --> 32:25.610
This one had really short hair.

32:25.693 --> 32:27.779
I mean, it was buzzed
nearly down to the scalp.

32:27.862 --> 32:30.490
Yeah, well, let's...
You know, let's forget about the haircut.

32:30.573 --> 32:33.660
I mean, if this kid had a buzz cut...

32:33.743 --> 32:35.119
could it be Lonnie's kid?

32:35.870 --> 32:38.164
Well, I...
I didn't get a good look at him.

32:40.166 --> 32:42.126
About the right height, though.

32:42.210 --> 32:43.878
I mean, could've been.

32:44.963 --> 32:46.631
Yeah, that's...

32:46.714 --> 32:47.715
Could've been.

32:49.634 --> 32:51.135
[sighs]

32:51.219 --> 32:53.930
Because I don't want to go by myself.

32:54.013 --> 32:57.183
Barb...
Barb, it's not rocket science.

32:57.266 --> 33:00.645
You just tell your parents you're gonna
stay at my place afterwards.

33:00.728 --> 33:03.606
No, tell them we're... studying.

33:03.690 --> 33:05.400
[Karen] Nancy! Dinner!

33:05.483 --> 33:07.193
Coming!

33:07.276 --> 33:09.946
Look, I gotta go.
I'll see you in an hour.

33:19.664 --> 33:21.290
Something wrong with the meatloaf?

33:22.166 --> 33:25.211
Oh, no, I had two
bologna sandwiches for lunch.

33:27.005 --> 33:28.006
I don't know why.

33:28.089 --> 33:29.966
[chuckles] Me, too.

33:31.175 --> 33:33.511
- It's delicious, Mommy.
- Thank you, sweetie.

33:34.345 --> 33:35.972
So, there's this...

33:36.055 --> 33:38.558
special assembly thing tonight...

33:38.641 --> 33:40.935
for Will at the school field.

33:41.019 --> 33:42.020
Barb's driving.

33:42.103 --> 33:44.272
Why am I just hearing about this?

33:45.148 --> 33:46.190
I thought you knew.

33:46.274 --> 33:49.360
I told you, I don't want you
out after dark until Will is found.

33:49.444 --> 33:52.780
I know, I know, but it'd be
super weird if I'm not there.

33:52.864 --> 33:54.907
I mean, everyone's going.

33:54.991 --> 33:55.992
[sighs]

33:58.161 --> 34:00.079
Just... be back by 10:00.

34:01.497 --> 34:02.665
Why don't you take the boys, too?

34:02.749 --> 34:03.958
- No!
- Mmm-mmm.

34:05.626 --> 34:07.712
Don't you think you should be there?
For Will?

34:10.423 --> 34:11.674
- [gasps]
- [Holly groans]

34:11.758 --> 34:14.010
Sorry. Spasm.

34:17.889 --> 34:20.141
- [Holly whimpers]
- Oh...

34:20.224 --> 34:21.434
It's okay, Holly.

34:21.517 --> 34:23.352
- It's just a loud noise.
- Nice.

34:25.063 --> 34:27.356
- [sirens wailing]
- [people shouting] Will!

34:29.442 --> 34:32.653
[volunteer] Better come out, buddy.
Will, where are ya?

34:42.997 --> 34:45.875
[Callahan] Hey, you think
Earl really saw Will?

34:45.958 --> 34:48.920
I mean, what's he doin'
with a shaved head?

34:49.003 --> 34:50.588
And stealing food from Benny?

34:50.671 --> 34:53.341
Tell you what,
when we find him, we'll ask.

34:53.424 --> 34:55.051
Can't ask a corpse questions.

34:55.134 --> 34:56.928
- [whistle blowing]
- [volunteer 2] Hold up!

34:57.011 --> 34:58.471
You got something?

35:01.641 --> 35:03.768
- Hey, what do you got?
- [Mr. Clarke] Not sure.

35:03.851 --> 35:05.770
Maybe nothing.

35:05.853 --> 35:07.772
I found this. In there.

35:12.485 --> 35:14.654
[Powell] No way a kid
crawls through there.

35:15.696 --> 35:17.406
[Hopper] I don't know...

35:17.490 --> 35:18.866
a scared enough one might.

35:18.950 --> 35:21.327
His brother said he was good at hiding.

35:44.475 --> 35:46.435
[rhythmic beeping]

35:52.817 --> 35:54.485
[radio static]

35:57.446 --> 35:58.447
[Mike] El?

36:04.245 --> 36:07.206
No adults.
Just us and some meatloaf.

36:10.668 --> 36:13.796
Don't worry.
They won't tell anyone about you.

36:13.880 --> 36:16.299
They promise.
Right?

36:16.382 --> 36:18.926
We never would've upset you
if we knew you had superpowers.

36:20.261 --> 36:21.304
[Dustin] Ow!

36:21.387 --> 36:26.017
What Dustin is trying to say
is that they were just scared... earlier.

36:26.100 --> 36:27.143
That's all.

36:27.226 --> 36:29.145
We just wanted to find our friend.

36:29.729 --> 36:30.771
"Friend"?

36:30.855 --> 36:33.733
Yeah, friend.
Will?

36:33.816 --> 36:37.111
What is "friend"?

36:37.195 --> 36:38.613
Is she serious?

36:41.282 --> 36:42.700
Um, a friend--

36:42.783 --> 36:44.535
Is someone that you'd do anything for.

36:44.619 --> 36:47.747
You lend them your cool stuff,
like comic books and trading cards.

36:47.830 --> 36:49.123
And they never break a promise.

36:49.207 --> 36:51.125
- Especially when there's spit.
- Spit?

36:51.209 --> 36:54.962
A spit swear means...
[spits] you never break your word.

36:55.046 --> 36:56.464
It's a bond.

36:56.547 --> 37:00.218
That's super important, because friends...

37:00.301 --> 37:02.553
they tell each other things.

37:02.637 --> 37:04.388
Things that parents don't know.

37:07.475 --> 37:09.560
[music playing on car radio]

37:11.229 --> 37:13.272
[Nancy] Barbara, pull over.
[Barbara] What?

37:13.356 --> 37:14.649
Pull over!

37:17.360 --> 37:19.237
What are we doing here?

37:19.320 --> 37:20.905
His house is three blocks away.

37:20.988 --> 37:22.448
We can't park in the driveway.

37:22.531 --> 37:23.574
Are you serious?

37:23.658 --> 37:24.784
Yeah, the neighbors might see.

37:24.867 --> 37:27.578
This is so stupid.
I'm just gonna drop you off.

37:27.662 --> 37:29.497
Calm down, Barb.
Come on.

37:29.580 --> 37:32.124
You promised that you'd go.
You're coming.

37:32.208 --> 37:33.459
We're gonna have a great time.

37:33.542 --> 37:35.086
He just wants to get in your pants.

37:35.169 --> 37:36.796
[chuckling] No, he doesn't.

37:36.879 --> 37:39.173
Nance... seriously.

37:40.299 --> 37:42.343
He invited you to his house.

37:42.969 --> 37:44.345
His parents aren't home.

37:45.012 --> 37:46.681
Come on, you are not this stupid.

37:46.764 --> 37:48.766
Tommy H. and Carol are gonna be there.

37:48.849 --> 37:51.936
Tommy and Carol have been
having sex since, like, seventh grade.

37:52.937 --> 37:54.897
It'll probably just be, like, a big orgy.

37:54.981 --> 37:57.942
- Gross.
- I'm serious!

37:58.025 --> 37:59.318
All right, well...

38:00.319 --> 38:03.572
you can be, like, my guardian. All right?

38:03.656 --> 38:06.117
Make sure I don't get drunk
and do anything stupid.

38:06.200 --> 38:07.201
Ugh.

38:10.538 --> 38:11.747
Is that a new bra?

38:13.416 --> 38:14.542
No.

38:15.876 --> 38:17.837
[music playing in distance]

38:22.758 --> 38:24.468
[doorbell rings]

38:27.305 --> 38:28.973
Barb, chill.

38:29.890 --> 38:31.267
I'm chill.

38:36.355 --> 38:37.732
Hello, ladies.

38:50.703 --> 38:51.746
[grunts]

39:09.847 --> 39:11.307
[Sandra] What are you doing?

39:12.308 --> 39:13.809
It's freezing.

39:19.690 --> 39:21.067
You ever feel cursed?

39:24.528 --> 39:27.573
You know, the last person
to go missing here was in, uh...

39:29.367 --> 39:30.951
the summer of '23.

39:32.620 --> 39:34.914
The last suicide was the fall of '61.

39:40.211 --> 39:42.671
When'd the last person freeze to death?

39:46.175 --> 39:48.386
Hey, come back inside.

39:48.469 --> 39:50.471
Warm me up. Just...

39:53.099 --> 39:54.683
Just give me a minute out here.

39:57.395 --> 39:58.729
[Sandra sighs]

40:21.377 --> 40:23.129
[Lucas] What's the weirdo doing?

40:29.176 --> 40:30.219
El?

40:43.816 --> 40:44.900
Will.

40:45.568 --> 40:46.569
Superpowers.

40:53.701 --> 40:56.620
Did you see him?
On Mirkwood?

40:58.038 --> 40:59.248
Do you know where he is?

41:15.139 --> 41:16.849
[Mike] I don't understand.

41:17.766 --> 41:18.934
Hiding.

41:19.059 --> 41:20.686
Will is hiding?

41:25.441 --> 41:27.026
From the bad men?

41:29.945 --> 41:31.614
Then from who?

41:42.416 --> 41:43.417
[sighs]

42:29.380 --> 42:31.173
[camera shutter clicking]

42:35.261 --> 42:36.804
Where are you?

42:44.270 --> 42:45.604
[camera shutter clicking]

42:52.528 --> 42:53.779
[camera shutter clicking]

42:53.862 --> 42:55.030
- [woman screaming]
- [gasps]

42:57.283 --> 42:58.826
[panting]

42:58.909 --> 43:00.828
[screaming continues]

43:05.874 --> 43:08.168
- [Carol shrieking]
- [Tommy] One! Two!

43:08.252 --> 43:10.921
- Three!
- [Carol] Stop it, Tommy, no! Don't!

43:11.005 --> 43:13.674
- [Tommy laughing]
- You're such an asshole, Tommy.

43:13.757 --> 43:15.217
[rock music playing]

43:23.892 --> 43:24.893
[exhales]

43:28.897 --> 43:30.608
Is that supposed to impress me?

43:31.400 --> 43:34.486
- You're not?
- You are a cliché, you do realize that?

43:34.570 --> 43:35.613
You are a cliché.

43:35.696 --> 43:38.115
What with your...
your grades and your band practice.

43:38.198 --> 43:39.617
[laughing] I'm so not in band.

43:39.700 --> 43:42.620
Okay, party girl. Why don't you just, uh,
show us how it's done, then?

43:42.703 --> 43:43.704
Okay.

43:50.836 --> 43:52.755
- You gotta make a little hole right in--
- I got it.

43:52.838 --> 43:55.049
Yeah, she's smart, you douche!

43:59.678 --> 44:01.805
Chug, chug, chug.

44:01.889 --> 44:03.349
[all chanting] Chug. Chug. Chug.

44:10.272 --> 44:11.565
[Tommy whooping]

44:11.649 --> 44:12.858
[laughing]

44:15.903 --> 44:17.154
Barb, you wanna try?

44:17.988 --> 44:19.531
What? No.

44:19.615 --> 44:20.866
No, I don't want to. Thanks.

44:20.949 --> 44:22.076
- Come on.
- [Steve] Yeah...

44:22.159 --> 44:23.494
- Come on. Yeah.
- [Barbara] Nance, I don't want to.

44:23.577 --> 44:25.287
- It's fun! Just give it a--
- Nance...

44:25.371 --> 44:27.039
Just... Just give it a shot.

44:29.249 --> 44:30.292
Okay.

44:35.881 --> 44:37.007
So you just...

44:39.343 --> 44:40.761
[Tommy chuckles]

44:41.720 --> 44:43.764
- Gnarly.
- [Nancy] Are you okay?

44:43.847 --> 44:45.307
- [Barbara] Yeah.
- Barb, you're bleeding.

44:45.391 --> 44:47.351
I'm fine.
Where's your bathroom?

44:47.434 --> 44:50.020
Oh, it's... It's, uh, down past
the kitchen, to the left.

44:50.104 --> 44:51.688
[Barbara] Okay. Thanks.

44:51.772 --> 44:52.981
[camera shutter clicking]

44:54.650 --> 44:56.193
[chuckling] Oh.

45:02.032 --> 45:03.575
[screams]

45:05.077 --> 45:08.205
Oh, my, God!
What the hell, Tommy?

45:08.288 --> 45:09.289
No!

45:10.916 --> 45:12.835
- [shrieks]
- [Steve] Whoo!

45:12.918 --> 45:14.878
[Tommy laughing]

45:25.681 --> 45:27.182
[all laughing]

45:27.808 --> 45:32.062
[camera shutter clicking]

45:36.525 --> 45:38.360
[camera shutter clicking]

45:51.331 --> 45:52.374
[phone rings]

45:53.000 --> 45:54.042
Hello?

45:56.253 --> 45:58.839
- Hello.
- [muffled breathing on phone]

45:58.922 --> 46:00.757
Who is this?
[stammers]

46:03.844 --> 46:06.096
- [whimpers] Will?
- [muffled breathing continues]

46:07.556 --> 46:10.309
- [indistinct noise over phone]
- [sobbing] Will, it's me.

46:10.392 --> 46:12.144
Talk to me.

46:12.227 --> 46:13.604
I'm here.

46:13.687 --> 46:15.564
Just tell me where you are, honey.

46:15.647 --> 46:17.608
- I can hear you. Please.
- [static]

46:18.609 --> 46:20.277
- [Will distorted] Mom?
- [gasps]

46:20.360 --> 46:21.737
Will!

46:21.820 --> 46:25.449
[sobbing] Yes, it's me.
It's me.

46:25.532 --> 46:27.826
Where are you? Where are you?
Just talk to me--

46:27.910 --> 46:30.412
- [electricity spiking]
- [screams]

46:30.496 --> 46:31.538
Oh, no, no!

46:31.622 --> 46:32.664
No!

46:32.748 --> 46:34.249
No!

46:34.333 --> 46:37.044
[sobbing] Oh, no! No, no...

46:39.922 --> 46:41.215
No!

46:43.217 --> 46:44.927
[sobbing continues]

46:47.304 --> 46:49.181
[screams] No!

46:52.434 --> 46:54.645
[wailing]

46:58.065 --> 47:00.067
[whimpering]

47:05.697 --> 47:07.074
Jonathan?

47:09.701 --> 47:10.702
[softly] What...

47:20.170 --> 47:21.797
- [music blares]
- [gasps]

47:21.880 --> 47:23.882
["Should I Stay or Should I Go"
playing on stereo]

47:25.759 --> 47:26.927
[whimpers]

47:28.095 --> 47:30.347
[music continues]

47:42.401 --> 47:43.443
[whispers] Will...

47:43.527 --> 47:45.571
[music continues]

47:54.162 --> 47:55.539
[electricity crackling]

47:55.622 --> 47:57.207
Will...

47:58.333 --> 48:00.002
[sobs] Will, is that you?

48:05.424 --> 48:06.508
[music stops]

48:07.467 --> 48:08.468
[whimpers]

48:13.974 --> 48:15.225
[screaming]

48:15.309 --> 48:16.643
[growling]

48:23.275 --> 48:24.651
[breathlessly] Oh, my God.

48:27.362 --> 48:28.947
[whimpering] Oh, God...

48:31.908 --> 48:34.036
Oh, my God...

48:34.119 --> 48:35.495
[engine starts]

48:35.579 --> 48:37.748
[music resumes playing]

48:37.831 --> 48:40.125
[electricity crackling]

48:49.468 --> 48:51.803
[music continues]

48:59.269 --> 49:00.854
[music continues]

49:18.246 --> 49:20.123
- [Tommy shudders]
- [Carol] I'm freezing.

49:20.207 --> 49:24.503
Hmm... well, I hear his
mom's room has a fireplace.

49:24.586 --> 49:25.837
[Steve] Are you kidding?
[Carol] Oh, yeah?

49:25.921 --> 49:28.256
Okay, well, you know,
you are cleaning the sheets.

49:28.340 --> 49:29.591
- You all right?
- Yeah.

49:29.675 --> 49:32.344
Yeah?
Come on, let's get you some dry clothes.

49:32.427 --> 49:33.595
[sighs]

49:37.891 --> 49:39.184
[Barbara] Nance!

49:39.309 --> 49:40.602
Nancy.

49:41.561 --> 49:43.313
Where are you going?

49:43.397 --> 49:44.439
Nowhere.

49:44.523 --> 49:46.358
Just... upstairs.

49:46.441 --> 49:48.068
To change.

49:48.151 --> 49:50.904
I... fell in the pool. [chuckles]

49:53.657 --> 49:55.534
Why don't you go ahead and go home.

49:55.617 --> 49:57.994
I'll just... I'll get a ride or something.

49:58.078 --> 49:59.454
Nance...

50:00.205 --> 50:01.915
Barb...

50:01.998 --> 50:03.583
I'm fine.

50:03.667 --> 50:06.086
This isn't you.

50:07.212 --> 50:08.839
I'm fine.

50:08.922 --> 50:12.509
Just... go ahead and go home, okay?

50:17.431 --> 50:18.473
[scoffs]

50:24.479 --> 50:25.522
[camera shutter clicks]

50:32.404 --> 50:33.655
Thanks.

50:36.575 --> 50:38.368
[inhales]

50:38.452 --> 50:39.995
Um...

50:40.078 --> 50:41.705
some privacy, maybe?

50:41.788 --> 50:43.290
[clicks tongue] Oh...

50:43.373 --> 50:45.000
Yeah, right.
Sorry. [chuckles]

50:49.755 --> 50:50.797
Steve?

51:04.811 --> 51:05.979
Damn.

51:06.104 --> 51:07.189
[chuckles]

51:08.315 --> 51:09.566
Shut up.

51:35.425 --> 51:39.679
[camera shutter clicking]

51:40.597 --> 51:42.140
[shutter jamming]

51:42.224 --> 51:44.184
[whirring]

52:14.756 --> 52:16.424
[electricity pulsating]

52:18.009 --> 52:19.386
[growls]

52:19.469 --> 52:21.096
- [roars]
- [Barbara shrieks]

53:00.302 --> 53:02.304
[rock music playing]
